<%--
Spinner

The template-side entry point to the application's spinner: place <Spinner /> and the
REGISTERED spinner component (Rsx.get_default_spinner()) renders inside it. From JS the
equivalent is $(element).component(Rsx.get_default_spinner()) on any host element.

THE HOST OWNS THE BOX, and it is a CENTERING STAGE - not a scale target. This wrapper
defaults to 60x60 via .Spinner in Spinner.scss, overridden by ordinary CSS wherever a
context wants another size (the form loading overlay hosts one at 150px); the
REGISTERED component decides whether it fills that box or draws at a fixed size
centered inside it. There are no size arguments anywhere.

Applications register their spinner once at init:

    class App_Spinner extends Component {
        static on_app_ready() { Rsx.set_default_spinner('App_Spinner'); }
        ...
    }
--%>
<Define:Spinner tag="div">
    <div class="Spinner__target" $sid="target"></div>
</Define:Spinner>
